        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2-\\sqrt5,\\ -2+\\sqrt5$",
          "worked": "At an $x$-intercept, $y=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+2)^2-5&=0\\\\(x+2)^2&=5\\\\x+2&=\\pm\\sqrt5\\\\x&=-2\\pm\\sqrt5\\end{align*}$$",
